{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3"],"declarations":88,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelve_prediction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelve_prediction","kind":"theorem","line":758,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L758-L762","doc":"**The `9₁₂` prediction.** Under `A_K^red = F_K`: `r = 17`, `|P_K| = 18`.\nUnverified — no independent count for `9₁₂` exists in the corpus — and stated\nwith its hypothesis, as the `(−2,3,7)` counterexample requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_rule_never_used_tetrahedra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_rule_never_used_tetrahedra","kind":"theorem","line":751,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L751-L756","doc":"**The rule is untouched**, because it reads the signature and never the\ntriangulation: `r = r₁ + 2r₂` by definition of `traceFieldDegree`, on every knot\nwhere it is stated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.tetrahedra_coincidence_breaks_at_nineTwelve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.tetrahedra_coincidence_breaks_at_nineTwelve","kind":"theorem","line":745,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L745-L749","doc":"**The coincidence BREAKS at `9₁₂`.** Ten ideal tetrahedra, degree-17 trace\nfield. So the rank rule cannot be a restatement of the triangulation count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelve_signature_gives_degree_seventeen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelve_signature_gives_degree_seventeen","kind":"theorem","line":741,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L741-L743","doc":"**The signature reproduces the stated degree 17** — a consistency check on\nthe transcription of a 17-term polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelveDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelveDegree","kind":"def","line":738,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L738-L739","doc":"Degree of `9₁₂`'s trace field, `r₁ + 2r₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelvePairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelvePairs","kind":"def","line":735,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L735-L736","doc":"Complex-conjugate pairs of embeddings of `9₁₂`'s trace field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelveReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelveReal","kind":"def","line":731,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L731-L733","doc":"`9₁₂`'s trace-field signature `[r₁, r₂] = [1, 8]`, DG §6.5 — the real-root\ncount verified independently here by exact Sturm sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelveTetrahedra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.nineTwelveTetrahedra","kind":"def","line":728,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L728-L729","doc":"`9₁₂`'s ideal-tetrahedron count (DG §6.5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.tetrahedra_match_degree_on_the_small_knots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.tetrahedra_match_degree_on_the_small_knots","kind":"theorem","line":722,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L722-L726","doc":"**The coincidence, on the three knots Parts F–H used.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.idealTetrahedra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.idealTetrahedra","kind":"def","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L715-L720","doc":"Ideal-tetrahedron counts, DG §6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sixOne_stokes_matrix_is_four_by_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sixOne_stokes_matrix_is_four_by_four","kind":"theorem","line":660,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L660-L666","doc":"**Structural prediction, stated so it can be falsified.** With `|P_K| = 5`\nboundary-parabolic representations, `6₁`'s reduced Stokes matrix is `4×4`, against\n`5₂`'s `3×3`. Not a DT count — the Stokes *constants* on those rays are still\nunpublished — but a definite shape for whoever computes them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.three_routes_agree_on_sixOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.three_routes_agree_on_sixOne","kind":"theorem","line":651,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L651-L658","doc":"**Three independent routes now give `r(6₁) = 4`**: the trace-field degree\n(DG, a number field), the geometric `A`-polynomial `L`-degree (Culler census, a\nNewton polygon), and the gluing-equation quartic's degree (Ohtsuki–Yokota, a\nsaddle-point analysis). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.gamma_is_not_rational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.gamma_is_not_rational","kind":"theorem","line":646,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L646-L649","doc":"**`γ` is not rational**, so the witness is genuinely degree-4 and not a\ndegenerate solution: its `α`, `α²`, `α³` components are all nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.gamma_powers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.gamma_powers","kind":"theorem","line":637,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L637-L644","doc":"The intermediate powers, recorded so a reader can check the certificate by\nhand: `γ² = −5α³ + 13α² − 12α − 7`, `γ³ = −13α³ + 33α² − 32α − 23`,\n`γ⁴ = −29α³ + 73α² − 64α − 55`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.saddle_field_equals_trace_field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.saddle_field_equals_trace_field","kind":"theorem","line":626,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L626-L635","doc":"**The isomorphism certificate, machine-checked.**\n`γ⁴ − γ³ − 4γ² + 4γ + 8 = 0` in `ℤ[α]/(dg)`. Its root `γ/2` is a root of\nOhtsuki–Yokota's gluing quartic `2z⁴ − z³ − 2z² + z + 1`, so that quartic has a\nroot in `ℚ(α)`; both being irreducible of degree 4, the fields coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.gamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.gamma","kind":"def","line":623,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L623-L624","doc":"The witness `γ = −α³ + 3α² − 4α − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.reduction_table_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.reduction_table_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L615-L621","doc":"**The reduction table is consistent**: `α·α³ = α⁴`, `α·α⁴ = α⁵`, `α·α⁵ = α⁶`.\nChecks the three constants against each other rather than trusting the\ntranscription. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.alpha","kind":"def","line":612,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L612-L613","doc":"`α` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.addAlg4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.addAlg4","kind":"def","line":608,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L608-L610","doc":"Sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.smulAlg4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.smulAlg4","kind":"def","line":605,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L605-L606","doc":"Scalar multiple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.mulAlg4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.mulAlg4","kind":"def","line":589,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L589-L603","doc":"Multiplication in `ℤ[α]/(dg)`: convolve, then fold `α⁴, α⁵, α⁶` back in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.a6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.a6","kind":"def","line":586,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L586-L587","doc":"`α⁶ = α³ − 10α² − 11α − 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.a5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.a5","kind":"def","line":583,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L583-L584","doc":"`α⁵ = 3α³ − 5α² − 7α − 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.a4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.a4","kind":"def","line":580,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L580-L581","doc":"Reduction of `α⁴`, from `dg(α) = 0`: `α⁴ = 2α³ − α² − 3α − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.Alg4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.Alg4","kind":"def","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L577-L578","doc":"An element of `ℤ[α]/(dg)` as `(c₀, c₁, c₂, c₃)` ↦ `c₀ + c₁α + c₂α² + c₃α³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.control_fires_where_hypothesis_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.control_fires_where_hypothesis_fails","kind":"theorem","line":520,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L520-L527","doc":"**The control fires at `(−2,3,7)`.** Its trace field is `5₂`'s, degree `3`,\nwhile its rank is `6` — the identity fails exactly where the hypothesis\n`A_K^red = F_K` fails. A rule that matched here too would be the worrying\noutcome. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.plus_one_leg_is_definitional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.plus_one_leg_is_definitional","kind":"theorem","line":514,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L514-L518","doc":"**The `+1` leg is not a test.** `full = geom + 1` holds definitionally here\n(the abelian representation), so it cannot corroborate anything — recorded so the\n`|P_K| = r + 1` agreement is never cited as evidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.the_three_degrees_are_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.the_three_degrees_are_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L508-L512","doc":"**The three values are distinct**, so the agreement is not a constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.degree_equals_geom_ldegree_on_all_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.degree_equals_geom_ldegree_on_all_three","kind":"theorem","line":500,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L500-L506","doc":"**Trace-field degree = geometric `L`-degree on all three certified knots.**\nA number field's degree and a Newton polygon's `L`-degree are unrelated a priori;\nthey agree at `2, 3, 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sixOne_prediction_confirmed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sixOne_prediction_confirmed","kind":"theorem","line":493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L493-L498","doc":"**The `6₁` prediction is confirmed.** The trace-field degree from DG's\nsignature `[0,2]` equals the certified geometric `L`-degree from the census. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.fullLDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.fullLDegree","kind":"def","line":490,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L490-L491","doc":"Full `A`-polynomial `L`-degree = geometric `+ 1` (the abelian factor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.geomLDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.geomLDegree","kind":"def","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L482-L488","doc":"Geometric `A`-polynomial `L`-degree, certified from the Culler census\n(sibling probe `apoly_census_ldegree_certification_probe.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.conditional_predictions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.conditional_predictions","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L429-L437","doc":"**The two conditional predictions.** Under `A_K^red = F_K`: `6₁` has rank `4`\nand `|P_K| = 5`; `(−2,3,9)` has rank `5` and `|P_K| = 6`. Not verified here — no\nsource in the corpus gives these ranks — and false if either knot has\nrepresentations outside its trace field, exactly as `(−2,3,7)` does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.trace_field_alone_fails_on_pretzel237","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.trace_field_alone_fails_on_pretzel237","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L421-L427","doc":"**And it FAILS for `(−2,3,7)`** — the worked counterexample. Its trace field\nis `5₂`'s, so the trace-field-only rule predicts `3`; the measured rank is `6`,\nbecause `P_K` acquires a second Galois orbit over `ℚ(η)`. This is why the\nhypothesis has to be stated, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.prediction_correct_where_hypothesis_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.prediction_correct_where_hypothesis_holds","kind":"theorem","line":415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L415-L419","doc":"**The hypothesis holds for `4₁` and `5₂`** — the prediction reproduces GZ's\nmeasured ranks `2` and `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.predictedRankFromTraceField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.predictedRankFromTraceField","kind":"def","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L412-L413","doc":"The rank predicted **under the hypothesis** `A_K^red = F_K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.dg_confirms_part4_inputs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.dg_confirms_part4_inputs","kind":"theorem","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L403-L410","doc":"**DG's types confirm Part 4's inputs on the two shared knots.** Part 4 read\nits signatures off GZ's prose; DG states them independently in `[r₁,r₂]`\nnotation, and they agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.signatures_match_polynomial_degrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.signatures_match_polynomial_degrees","kind":"theorem","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L394-L401","doc":"**The signatures reproduce the stated minimal-polynomial degrees.** A\nconsistency check on the transcription: `[0,1] → 2`, `[1,1] → 3`, `[0,2] → 4`,\n`[1,2] → 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.traceFieldDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.traceFieldDegree","kind":"def","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L390-L392","doc":"Degree of the trace field, `r₁ + 2r₂` — checkable against the stated minimal\npolynomials (degrees `2, 3, 4, 5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.traceFieldPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.traceFieldPairs","kind":"def","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L383-L388","doc":"`r₂`, the number of **complex-conjugate pairs** of embeddings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.traceFieldReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.traceFieldReal","kind":"def","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L376-L381","doc":"`r₁`, the number of **real** embeddings of the trace field (DG type `[r₁,r₂]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.instDecidableEqDGKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.instDecidableEqDGKnot","kind":"instance","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L374-L374","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.pretzel239","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.pretzel239","kind":"ctor","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L373-L373","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.sixOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.sixOne","kind":"ctor","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L372-L372","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.fiveTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.fiveTwo","kind":"ctor","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L371-L371","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.fourOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot.fourOne","kind":"ctor","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L370-L370","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.DGKnot","kind":"inductive","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L368-L374","doc":"The knots for which Dimofte–Garoufalidis §6 gives a trace-field signature. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sign_question_only_arises_at_level_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sign_question_only_arises_at_level_two","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L312-L319","doc":"**At level 1 there is no group, hence no sign block to be absent.** The\n`Γ/Γ(N)` quotient is trivial exactly when `N = 1`, so `4₁` and `5₂` supply no\ncomparandum — the sign-absence is a one-knot statement among these three, and\nsaying otherwise would overstate it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.level","kind":"def","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L305-L310","doc":"The level `N` of each knot (GZ §3.5: the level is *introduced* at `(−2,3,7)`,\nwhich has `N = 2`; the other two are `N = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_sign_multiplicity_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_sign_multiplicity_zero","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L300-L301","doc":"**The instance follows.** `W₀` itself has zero sign multiplicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sign_absence_is_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.sign_absence_is_forced","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L291-L298","doc":"**The sign block's absence is FORCED, for the whole family.** Starting from\nthe permutation character (sign multiplicity `0`) and adding *any* number of\ntrivial summands leaves it `0`. So no representation of the form\n`ℂ[3 points] ⊕ ℂ^{⊕n}` — which is what `W₀` is — can contain the sign\nrepresentation. Not \"observed to be zero\": zero by shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.addTrivial_preserves_signMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.addTrivial_preserves_signMult","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L285-L289","doc":"**Adding a trivial summand does not change the sign multiplicity.** This is\nthe whole mechanism: `χ_triv = (1,1,1)` contributes `1 − 3 + 2 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.signMult6_matches_ip6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.signMult6_matches_ip6","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L282-L283","doc":"`signMult6` agrees with `ip6 · chiSign` on the permutation character. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.signMult6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.signMult6","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L278-L280","doc":"Six times the **sign multiplicity** of a character given by its three class\nvalues `(a₀, a₁, a₂)`: `1·a₀·1 + 3·a₁·(−1) + 2·a₂·1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_dimension_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_dimension_four","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L275-L276","doc":"`W₀` has the dimension Part A extracted: `χ(e) = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_is_perm_plus_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_is_perm_plus_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L271-L273","doc":"**`W₀` is a permutation module plus a trivial**, at the level of characters —\nand characters determine complex representations up to isomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiW0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiW0","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L268-L269","doc":"The character of `W₀` as GZ decomposes it: standard `⊕` trivial`²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.perm_has_no_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.perm_has_no_sign","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L264-L266","doc":"**A permutation module on 3 points contains no sign component.** This is the\ngeneral fact the absence rests on — nothing about knots enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.perm_is_trivial_plus_standard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.perm_is_trivial_plus_standard","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L259-L262","doc":"**The permutation module on 3 points is `trivial ⊕ standard`.** Multiplicity\none each (`6⟨·,·⟩ = 6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.addChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.addChar","kind":"def","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L256-L257","doc":"Pointwise sum of characters (direct sum of representations). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.ip6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.ip6","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L252-L254","doc":"Six times the character inner product, kept integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiPerm","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L249-L250","doc":"Character of the permutation module on 3 points (`χ(g) = #` fixed points). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiStandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiStandard","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L246-L247","doc":"Character of the 2-dimensional standard representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiSign","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L243-L244","doc":"Character of the sign representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiTrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.chiTrivial","kind":"def","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L240-L241","doc":"Character of the trivial representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.s3ClassSizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.s3ClassSizes","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L237-L238","doc":"Class sizes of `S₃`: identity, transpositions, 3-cycles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.level_two_confined_to_w0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.level_two_confined_to_w0","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L194-L200","doc":"**The level-2 behaviour is confined to `W₀`.** `ρ` is the identity on `W₁`\nand `W₂`, so the entire `Γ(2)` phenomenon lives in the 4-dimensional weight space\n— exactly the one whose multiplicity the prose misreported. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_has_no_sign_representation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_has_no_sign_representation","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L188-L192","doc":"**The sign representation is absent from `W₀`.** Under the standard\nidentification the sign block is the bar-odd one, so the `Γ/Γ(2)` action on the\nlevel-2 part of the third knot's grading carries **no** sign component — a\nchirality-flavoured statement, and the one asymmetry in the decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_decomposition_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0_decomposition_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L180-L186","doc":"**The decomposition is dimensionally consistent**: `2·1 + 1·2 + 0·1 = 4 =\ndim W₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0Multiplicities","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.w0Multiplicities","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L176-L178","doc":"The multiplicity of each `S₃`-irrep in `W₀`, in the same `(3) / (2,1) /\n(1,1,1)` order: two trivials, one standard, **no sign**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.s3IrrepDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.s3IrrepDims","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L172-L174","doc":"The irreducible representations of `S₃`, as partitions of `3`, with their\ndimensions: `(3)` trivial, `(2,1)` standard, `(1,1,1)` sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.ranks_are_three_distinct_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.ranks_are_three_distinct_values","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L153-L158","doc":"The three ranks are distinct, so the agreement is not a two-point fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_from_signature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_from_signature","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L147-L151","doc":"**The signature formula predicts the rank directly**: real embeddings plus\ntwice the complex-conjugate pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_eq_pk_minus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_eq_pk_minus_one","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L142-L145","doc":"**`r = |P_K| − 1` on all three knots.** The grading counts exactly the\nnon-trivial boundary-parabolic representations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.higher_multiplicity_does_not_refute_h_ad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.higher_multiplicity_does_not_refute_h_ad","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L125-L133","doc":"**The guard, stated so it cannot be lost.** The `(−2,3,7)` grading *is*\nnon-multiplicity-free — a weight of dimension `4` — yet this does **not** refute\n`H_Ad`, because the graded object is not the one `s(x)` describes. Recording both\nhalves together is the point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.weight_set_is_knot_dependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.weight_set_is_knot_dependent","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L115-L123","doc":"**Check 2 — even the weight *set* is knot-dependent.** `4₁` grades a\n**2**-element set, `(−2,3,7)` a **3**-element one; and `4₁`'s weights are\nhalf-integers while `(−2,3,7)`'s are integers (GZ's \"level\" phenomenon). A\nknot-independent core cannot be read off a grading that changes shape per knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.fourOneWeightsDoubled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.fourOneWeightsDoubled","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L111-L113","doc":"The `4₁` weight set: GZ §3.4 declares `g₀, g₁` to have weights `∓1/2`\n(recorded doubled, as `∓1`, to stay in `Int`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_total_differs_from_s_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank_total_differs_from_s_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L103-L109","doc":"**Check 1 — the totals disagree already at `4₁`.** The grading's total is\n`r = 2` there, while `s(1) = 3`. A grading of a 2-dimensional space cannot be the\n3-term polynomial `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.rank","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L95-L101","doc":"The rank `r` of each knot: GZ §3.4 gives `2r` q-series in total, and reports\n`4`, `6`, `12` for `4₁`, `5₂`, `(−2,3,7)`. (GZ 2111.06645 §2.1 states the same\nranks `2, 3, 6` directly.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.totals_agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.totals_agree","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L85-L88","doc":"Both readings agree on the **total**, which is why the slip is easy to miss:\nit is a transposition, not a miscount. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.prose_contradicts_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.prose_contradicts_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L77-L83","doc":"**The erratum, as a theorem.** The prose dimensions differ from what the\npaper's own decomposition and `δ`-degrees give — and differ precisely by\ntransposing the first two entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.hweights_match_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.hweights_match_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**The centred weight vector reproduces it too**, weight `−1` playing the role\nof degree `0`. Two independent encodings of the same grading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.delta_matches_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.delta_matches_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L66-L69","doc":"**The `δ` degrees reproduce the explicit decomposition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.proseDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.proseDims","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The dimensions the **prose** sentence states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.decompositionDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.decompositionDims","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L59-L61","doc":"Dimensions of `W₀, W₁, W₂` as the explicit decomposition gives them:\n`W₀ = ⟨H₀,H₃,H₄,H₅⟩`, `W₁ = ⟨H₁⟩`, `W₂ = ⟨H₂⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.mult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.mult","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L56-L57","doc":"Multiplicity of a weight in a grading vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.hWeights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.hWeights","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The companion weight vector on `h = (h_j)_{j=0}^{5}` (GZ §3.5), the same\ngrading centred so the weights are `{−1, 0, +1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.deltaDegrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZThirdKnotRankGrading.deltaDegrees","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZThirdKnotRankGrading.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The ε-deformation degree `δ_j` of each of the six `(−2,3,7)` q-series\n(GZ §3.5, eq. (3.17) preamble). ","signatureChunk":0}]}